## FAST API async (production server):


Gunicorn + Uvicorn workers (recommended for production)
The optimal setup is both together:


Gunicorn (process manager) → Uvicorn workers (async)

gunicorn src.main:app \
  --worker-class uvicorn.workers.UvicornWorker \
  --workers 4 \
  --bind 0.0.0.0:8000
Why not Uvicorn alone?
Feature	Uvicorn alone	Gunicorn + Uvicorn
Async handling	Yes	Yes
Process management	Basic	Production-grade
Worker crash recovery	No	Yes — auto restarts
Graceful reload	No	Yes
Worker memory limits	No	Yes
Battle-tested process manager	No	Yes
Uvicorn alone is fine for development but has no supervisor — if a worker crashes, it stays dead.

Update your Dockerfile

CMD ["gunicorn", "src.main:app", \
     "--worker-class", "uvicorn.workers.UvicornWorker", \
     "--workers", "4", \
     "--bind", "0.0.0.0:8000", \
     "--timeout", "120", \
     "--keep-alive", "5"]
Add gunicorn to pyproject.toml:


uv add gunicorn
Summary
Uvicorn alone — development only
Gunicorn + UvicornWorker — production standard for FastAPI
FastAPI's own documentation recommends this combination for production deployments.

