## Development mode

can you use gunicorn and uvicorn for dev server from the very starting
No — Gunicorn doesn't support --reload (hot reload) well, which makes it painful for development.

Recommended setup
Environment	Command
Development	uvicorn src.main:app --reload
Production	gunicorn src.main:app --worker-class uvicorn.workers.UvicornWorker --workers 4
Why not Gunicorn for dev?
--reload (auto-restart on file change) only works with Uvicorn directly
Gunicorn spawns multiple processes — harder to read logs and debug
Slower startup for every code change
Standard pattern — two Dockerfiles
Dockerfile (production — what you already have):


CMD ["gunicorn", "src.main:app", \
     "--worker-class", "uvicorn.workers.UvicornWorker", \
     "--workers", "4", \
     "--bind", "0.0.0.0:8000"]
Dockerfile.dev (development):


CMD ["uvicorn", "src.main:app", "--host", "0.0.0.0", "--port", "8000", "--reload"]
Or just run Uvicorn directly on the host without Docker for dev:


uv run uvicorn src.main:app --reload
This is the same pattern FastAPI's own documentation recommends.